00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:23.491
you have massive clarity
and endless motivation.

00:10:23.491 --> 00:10:25.686
When you have fuzzy thinking,

00:10:25.686 --> 00:10:28.738
it's so hard to take big action.

00:10:28.738 --> 00:10:31.391
And complexity is the
enemy of real execution.

00:10:31.391 --> 00:10:33.166
The more complex you make something,

00:10:33.166 --> 00:10:35.096
the less likely you are
to take action, right?

00:10:35.096 --> 00:10:35.968
That's number one.

00:10:35.968 --> 00:10:38.704
Number two, strategically scheduling

00:10:38.704 --> 00:10:40.426
everything in your schedule.

00:10:40.426 --> 00:10:41.617
Your schedule is a reflection

00:10:41.617 --> 00:10:43.666
of your integrity and priorities.

00:10:43.666 --> 00:10:45.791
When I see people flying
by the cuff of their pants,

00:10:45.791 --> 00:10:49.886
not strategically thinking
things through, I just think

00:10:49.886 --> 00:10:52.406
their business is going
to eventually shut down,

00:10:52.406 --> 00:10:54.328
because you can only do that so far.

00:10:54.328 --> 00:10:56.221
You have to really be intentional.

00:10:56.221 --> 00:10:59.164
Number three is seizing
and maximizing each day.

00:10:59.164 --> 00:11:01.590
If you don't make the most of your days,

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:03.983
you'll never have
amazing weeks and months.

00:11:03.983 --> 00:11:05.928
But if you make the most of your days,

00:11:05.928 --> 00:11:09.314
the weeks and months take
care of themselves, right?

00:11:09.314 --> 00:11:11.021
Fourth, staying intentional.

00:11:11.021 --> 00:11:14.299
Those who are outcome-focused
and result-focused

00:11:14.299 --> 00:11:17.791
and are intentional produce
results like nobody else.

00:11:17.791 --> 00:11:19.729
And lastly, for me, this was the big one,

00:11:19.729 --> 00:11:22.996
your success environment
and success orientation.

00:11:22.996 --> 00:11:25.973
Most people are controlled
by everything external

00:11:25.973 --> 00:11:27.698
and they're never fully in control

00:11:27.698 --> 00:11:29.723
of exactly where they want to go.

00:11:29.723 --> 00:11:32.909
But the achievers are always
focused on being in control

00:11:32.909 --> 00:11:35.910
of their agenda and not
letting other people interrupt

00:11:35.910 --> 00:11:38.935
their productivity, their
mindset, their standards

00:11:38.935 --> 00:11:40.272
and where they're going.

00:11:40.272 --> 00:11:42.604
So, that's the five, so
we can definitely dive in.

00:11:42.604 --> 00:11:45.607
So, the first thing is absolute clarity.

00:11:45.607 --> 00:11:49.413
We talked a little on the
last episode that we did

00:11:49.413 --> 00:11:52.457
on absolute clarity, but I want
to dive a little bit deeper.

00:11:52.457 --> 00:11:54.416
You have to learn how to master yourself

00:11:54.416 --> 00:11:56.240
and know how to spark your own fire.

00:11:56.240 --> 00:11:59.870
The more you have to count on
someone else to motivate you,

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:02.804
the less money you'll make and
the less effective you'll be.

00:12:02.804 --> 00:12:06.614
So learn how to master yourself,
how to spark your own fire.

00:12:06.614 --> 00:12:10.423
And how I did that was I put
my plan, I put my vision,

00:12:10.423 --> 00:12:15.412
I put my values and my reasons
and my goals, on one page.

00:12:15.412 --> 00:12:18.229
Whew, and I, literally, Evan, I have

00:12:18.229 --> 00:12:20.607
this is from 2015, but I...

00:12:20.607 --> 00:12:21.440
- There's the page.

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:22.870
- Yeah, but I have like
five or six of them

00:12:22.870 --> 00:12:24.491
that I redo every couple months,

00:12:24.491 --> 00:12:26.739
but it's like I've done this since 2012.

00:12:26.739 --> 00:12:29.121
I had it in the shower, above the shower.

00:12:29.121 --> 00:12:29.954
- It's laminated.

00:12:29.954 --> 00:12:30.787
I love it.

00:12:30.787 --> 00:12:31.620
- It's laminated.

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:32.836
But let me tell you what's on that page,

00:12:32.836 --> 00:12:35.192
because it's such a game changer for me.

00:12:35.192 --> 00:12:37.525
First is your ideal outcome.

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:40.496
A lot of people don't even
know their ideal outcome

00:12:40.496 --> 00:12:43.040
of what they want to accomplish
in the next six months.

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:45.291
If I ask a hundred
entrepreneurs, hey, what is the

00:12:45.291 --> 00:12:48.009
ideal outcome for you and your business?

00:12:48.009 --> 00:12:49.236
How many hours are you working?

00:12:49.236 --> 00:12:50.472
How much money are you bringing in?

00:12:50.472 --> 00:12:52.319
What's your subscribers look like?

00:12:52.319 --> 00:12:54.503
How involved are you
in the business, right?

00:12:54.503 --> 00:12:56.017
How big is your team?

00:12:56.017 --> 00:12:58.457
What exactly are your marketing tactics?

00:12:58.457 --> 00:13:01.031
They're like, I have no idea.

00:13:01.031 --> 00:13:04.373
99 out of a hundred don't know.

00:13:04.373 --> 00:13:05.734
So what's your ideal outcome?

00:13:05.734 --> 00:13:08.871
And don't base this off
your past or limitations.

00:13:08.871 --> 00:13:12.151
Base this off what's possible
and your potential, right?

00:13:12.151 --> 00:13:13.573
So just a simple paragraph.

00:13:13.573 --> 00:13:14.437
What's your ideal outcome?

00:13:14.437 --> 00:13:16.672
I don't really like to
say vision statement,

00:13:16.672 --> 00:13:18.651
'cause that's over-talked
about and over-played,

00:13:18.651 --> 00:13:21.499
but I like to tell people
it's your ideal outcome.

00:13:21.499 --> 00:13:24.543
So once you have that on top, then,

00:13:24.543 --> 00:13:26.545
this is big, your core values.

00:13:26.545 --> 00:13:29.387
What are most important to
you in life and business?

00:13:29.387 --> 00:13:31.690
Because you want to build a
business around your values,

00:13:31.690 --> 00:13:34.328
not settle for a business that
doesn't match your values,

00:13:34.328 --> 00:13:36.632
because then you're living
incongruently, right?

00:13:36.632 --> 00:13:37.806
And people do this all the time.

00:13:37.806 --> 00:13:42.714
But in the new economy,
in 2017, there's no reason

00:13:42.714 --> 00:13:45.514
why you can't create and
design your ideal lifestyle

00:13:45.514 --> 00:13:47.790
or be picky and choosy with your business

00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:49.456
because you're becoming so valuable.

00:13:49.456 --> 00:13:50.289
So values.

00:13:50.289 --> 00:13:53.595
For me, it's family, freedom, autonomy,

00:13:53.595 --> 00:13:56.660
and then legacy and
impact, even before income.

00:13:56.660 --> 00:13:59.395
People always say, well what about income?

00:13:59.395 --> 00:14:01.982
It's like, yeah, that's
very important to me,

00:14:01.982 --> 00:14:03.828
but I have leverage where
I don't need income.

00:14:03.828 --> 00:14:08.269
So what's cool for me
is, my values are intact

00:14:08.269 --> 00:14:09.997
to where I can say yes
and no to any opportunity

00:14:09.997 --> 00:14:11.609
that comes to me based on my values.

00:14:11.609 --> 00:14:13.686
Like, I've turned down speeches, Evan,

00:14:13.686 --> 00:14:15.682
for close to 10 grand.

00:14:15.682 --> 00:14:17.120
One was in Chicago in January.

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:18.851
That's enough to turn
anything down in Chicago,

00:14:18.851 --> 00:14:20.268
'cause it's freezing.

00:14:20.268 --> 00:14:21.442
Sorry to all the Chicago people.

00:14:21.442 --> 00:14:22.403
You probably agree.

00:14:22.403 --> 00:14:25.503
But anyways, I turn down
speeches that are well-paid,

00:14:25.503 --> 00:14:27.624
and I've done three
speeches in the inner city

00:14:27.624 --> 00:14:29.814
in LA for underprivileged kids.

00:14:29.814 --> 00:14:31.893
Now if my values were number one, money,

00:14:31.893 --> 00:14:34.087
I'd probably turn down the free speeches

00:14:34.087 --> 00:14:35.194
and do all the paid ones,

00:14:35.194 --> 00:14:37.330
but my value's impact and giving back.

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:39.494
So you got to define what your values are.

00:14:39.494 --> 00:14:41.769
After that, it's your top five goals.

00:14:41.769 --> 00:14:44.707
So what are the big five
for the next six months?

00:14:44.707 --> 00:14:47.464
And I'll kind of run
through this kind of quick,

00:14:47.464 --> 00:14:48.852
but what are the five things that you want

00:14:48.852 --> 00:14:50.888
to accomplish and get done
in the next six months?

00:14:50.888 --> 00:14:53.671
And then underneath that, it's
your most powerful reasons.

00:14:53.671 --> 00:14:55.752
What are the reasons that drive you?

00:14:55.752 --> 00:14:58.063
What are your top five
most compelling reasons,

00:14:58.063 --> 00:14:59.787
'cause this is the fuel that gets you

00:14:59.787 --> 00:15:02.871
to take action on the top five.

00:15:02.871 --> 00:15:04.221
So what are your five biggest reasons?

00:15:04.221 --> 00:15:06.755
You might have to write down
like 20 or 30 and simplify

00:15:06.755 --> 00:15:08.871
to get to the ones that mean something,

00:15:08.871 --> 00:15:10.746
but if you don't have,
if you're not waking up

00:15:10.746 --> 00:15:13.338
at four or five in the
morning fired up and excited,

00:15:13.338 --> 00:15:15.784
your reasons aren't strong enough.

00:15:15.784 --> 00:15:16.699
I'm serious.

00:15:16.699 --> 00:15:18.385
So get some strong reasons of why

00:15:18.385 --> 00:15:19.953
you want to do what you do.

00:15:19.953 --> 00:15:24.200
And lastly, what's your one
key skill or one key habit

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:26.740
that's most relevant to
your six-month vision

00:15:26.740 --> 00:15:28.324
that you're going to focus on for the next

00:15:28.324 --> 00:15:29.832
month or two until it's mastered?

00:15:29.832 --> 00:15:31.847
You see, one big part
of productivity, Evan,

00:15:31.847 --> 00:15:34.696
is focusing on mastery versus overload.

00:15:34.696 --> 00:15:36.215
There's so much information.

00:15:36.215 --> 00:15:37.545
There's all this technology.

00:15:37.545 --> 00:15:40.868
There's podcasts, YouTube,
audios, videos, books,

00:15:40.868 --> 00:15:43.184
trainings, seminars, and
a lot of entrepreneurs

00:15:43.184 --> 00:15:45.166
use it as a cop out,
to where they're like,

00:15:45.166 --> 00:15:47.049
oh, I want to keep learning and growing,

00:15:47.049 --> 00:15:50.113
and instead of executing
on what they already know,

00:15:50.113 --> 00:15:51.578
they want to learn more, and say,

00:15:51.578 --> 00:15:52.578
well, I'm still studying.

00:15:52.578 --> 00:15:53.411
No, no, no.

00:15:53.411 --> 00:15:56.008
You need to execute and
get addicted to outcomes,

00:15:56.008 --> 00:15:57.686
not just information.

00:15:57.686 --> 00:15:59.624
So now you measure
everything you're studying

00:15:59.624 --> 00:16:02.206
against this one-page productivity plan,

00:16:02.206 --> 00:16:04.745
and if you do that, it
gives you so much clarity.

00:16:04.745 --> 00:16:07.567
Now the goal is to let
your vision guide you,

00:16:07.567 --> 00:16:09.588
not your current circumstances, right?

00:16:09.588 --> 00:16:11.444
So that's the first thing,
is just simplifying.

00:16:11.444 --> 00:16:12.679
Do you have any questions
or do you want me to answer

00:16:12.679 --> 00:16:15.668
any of the subscribers'
or fans' questions,

00:16:15.668 --> 00:16:16.813
I'd be happy to.

00:16:16.813 --> 00:16:17.777
- Yeah, let's do it.

00:16:17.777 --> 00:16:19.905
First off, loved all the
value, man, it's great.

00:16:19.905 --> 00:16:21.949
You're just firin' it at us.

00:16:21.949 --> 00:16:22.943
I love it.

00:16:22.943 --> 00:16:24.883
I'm trying to keep track
of all the comments.

00:16:24.883 --> 00:16:27.214
It's nuts with all the
questions coming in.

00:16:27.214 --> 00:16:29.093
- Give me the weirdest one.

00:16:29.093 --> 00:16:29.926
I'm just kidding.

00:16:29.926 --> 00:16:32.187
- The weirdest one?

00:16:32.187 --> 00:16:33.710
Um. The weirdest one.

00:16:33.710 --> 00:16:34.543
- Don't.

00:16:34.543 --> 00:16:35.376
It's going to be way too weird.

00:16:35.376 --> 00:16:36.249
- Okay, you know what?

00:16:36.249 --> 00:16:37.354
Actually, people want to know exactly

00:16:37.354 --> 00:16:39.486
what time we wake up.

00:16:39.486 --> 00:16:40.918
- Oooh. Good question.

00:16:40.918 --> 00:16:45.085
So, here's the, I used to be
obsessed with the exact time.

00:16:46.196 --> 00:16:48.691
When you're in a successful
state of mind, I've been around,

00:16:48.691 --> 00:16:50.978
I've been very fortunate to
be around a lot of seven,

00:16:50.978 --> 00:16:54.477
eight, nine figure earners,
very, very successful people.

00:16:54.477 --> 00:16:57.139
I was with Ryan Blair at
his house two days ago.

00:16:57.139 --> 00:16:57.972
Do you know Ryan?

00:16:57.972 --> 00:16:58.805
I think you did a...
- Yeah.

00:16:58.805 --> 00:17:02.972
Yeah, and he sold a company
for 782 million dollars.

00:17:04.875 --> 00:17:06.934
That, I can't conceptualize that,

00:17:06.934 --> 00:17:09.939
selling a company and getting
that much, but I noticed,

00:17:09.939 --> 00:17:11.020
and I noticed from a lot of people,

00:17:11.020 --> 00:17:13.239
it's not about exactly when you wake up.

00:17:13.239 --> 00:17:16.457
It's about what you do when you're awake

00:17:16.457 --> 00:17:18.086
and how productive you are.

00:17:18.086 --> 00:17:19.378
So for me it's different.

00:17:19.378 --> 00:17:21.519
If I'm traveling and
speaking, I'll wake up

00:17:21.519 --> 00:17:24.872
at different times, but
in my sacrifice stages,

00:17:24.872 --> 00:17:28.404
like when I was in my early, early 20s,

00:17:28.404 --> 00:17:29.353
I wouldn't get much sleep.

00:17:29.353 --> 00:17:31.512
I'd get five, five-and-a-half, six hours,

00:17:31.512 --> 00:17:33.967
because I'd be hustling
and grinding, sacrificing.

00:17:33.967 --> 00:17:36.112
Now that I've built the foundation,

00:17:36.112 --> 00:17:38.416
I like to get seven to eight hours.

00:17:38.416 --> 00:17:40.670
You ask me five, six
years ago, I would say,

00:17:40.670 --> 00:17:42.134
you don't need eight
hours, you're a hustler.

00:17:42.134 --> 00:17:42.967
You need four hours.

00:17:42.967 --> 00:17:44.089
Forget sleep.

00:17:44.089 --> 00:17:47.017
That's just not smart,
'cause productivity,

00:17:47.017 --> 00:17:48.148
you need to have the right sleep.

00:17:48.148 --> 00:17:50.021
But it depends on what stage you're at.

00:17:50.021 --> 00:17:52.994
And to be honest, figure
out when you're in the zone

00:17:52.994 --> 00:17:55.102
and when you're most creative

00:17:55.102 --> 00:17:56.549
and when you have the most willpower.

00:17:56.549 --> 00:18:00.133
I know people, Evan, that
go to bed at two or three.

00:18:00.133 --> 00:18:02.721
Like one of my friends
who's a recording artist,

00:18:02.721 --> 00:18:05.606
he is the most productive
from eleven to three

00:18:05.606 --> 00:18:09.410
in the morning, and then
he'll get up at ten or eleven.

00:18:09.410 --> 00:18:11.692
I know some people who
conk out and go to bed

00:18:11.692 --> 00:18:16.057
at nine or ten, and they're
productive from four to eight.

00:18:16.057 --> 00:18:19.071
So it really, it's not about
exactly what time you wake up,

00:18:19.071 --> 00:18:22.124
it's about when you're most
effective and productive,

00:18:22.124 --> 00:18:26.446
and delegating all your
highest-value, most profit-producing

00:18:26.446 --> 00:18:28.951
activities to that time.

00:18:28.951 --> 00:18:31.539
So don't get on the subject of what time,

00:18:31.539 --> 00:18:33.628
get on the subject of what you're doing

00:18:33.628 --> 00:18:36.347
and is that your most productive hours?

00:18:36.347 --> 00:18:37.785
Good question, though.

00:18:37.785 --> 00:18:38.618
And that's changed.

00:18:38.618 --> 00:18:40.520
That would've been a
different answer years ago.

00:18:40.520 --> 00:18:43.645
- Yeah, and parenthood
changes that, too, as well.

00:18:43.645 --> 00:18:44.478
- Exactly.

00:18:44.478 --> 00:18:46.115
I don't want to know about that yet.

00:18:46.115 --> 00:18:49.948
- For me, usually I start
to get ready for bed

00:18:51.715 --> 00:18:55.349
around eleven, and then I'll read in bed

00:18:55.349 --> 00:18:57.599
and hang out with the wife,

00:18:59.309 --> 00:19:00.905
and then kind of asleep by midnight,

00:19:00.905 --> 00:19:03.773
and then awake at
seven-something, typically.

00:19:03.773 --> 00:19:05.165
- Let me ask you this.

00:19:05.165 --> 00:19:08.794
When do you feel like, out
of the 24 hours in a day,

00:19:08.794 --> 00:19:11.577
when do you feel like your most productive

00:19:11.577 --> 00:19:13.807
three or four hours are,
where you're like super

00:19:13.807 --> 00:19:15.555
in the zone and hyper-focused?

00:19:15.555 --> 00:19:19.602
Is it like, morning,
evening, what do you think?

00:19:19.602 --> 00:19:22.102
- My default would be evening,

00:19:24.009 --> 00:19:27.959
but after my morning
routine, and I love what you,

00:19:27.959 --> 00:19:28.792
what did you say last time?

00:19:28.792 --> 00:19:30.330
You had like a champion's
routine or something,

00:19:30.330 --> 00:19:32.791
what did you call it?

00:19:32.791 --> 00:19:34.120
- Prizefighter routine.

00:19:34.120 --> 00:19:35.687
- Prizefighter routine, it was great.

00:19:35.687 --> 00:19:36.620
I like that.
- In the morning, yeah.

00:19:36.620 --> 00:19:40.376
After I go to my morning routine, I'm set.

00:19:40.376 --> 00:19:42.642
So after I do all that stuff, then I'm set

00:19:42.642 --> 00:19:44.377
for whatever I'm going to do next.

00:19:44.377 --> 00:19:45.898
- That's my productive time, too.

00:19:45.898 --> 00:19:47.174
It's right after my morning routine.

00:19:47.174 --> 00:19:49.722
I have the most adrenaline,
the most energy.

00:19:49.722 --> 00:19:51.442
I'm in the right state of
mind, so that's where I place

00:19:51.442 --> 00:19:55.510
my highest-value activities,
is that first 60 minutes

00:19:55.510 --> 00:19:57.799
after my morning routine, so I love it.

00:19:57.799 --> 00:19:59.836
We're pretty similar in that sense.

00:19:59.836 --> 00:20:01.181
So you want to?
- Okay, let's see what's...

00:20:01.181 --> 00:20:02.158
Oh, go ahead.

00:20:02.158 --> 00:20:02.991
- No, let's see what's next.

00:20:02.991 --> 00:20:05.587
It's like the questions are coming in,

00:20:05.587 --> 00:20:09.401
and we answered one, Peter,
so we got to be productive.

00:20:09.401 --> 00:20:12.122
- I'll probably answer a
lot of them in the next

00:20:12.122 --> 00:20:15.737
couple tips, but we can keep answering.

00:20:15.737 --> 00:20:17.940
- A lot of them you have
already covered in the tips

00:20:17.940 --> 00:20:19.206
as well, but I think you could go a little

00:20:19.206 --> 00:20:22.244
deeper with some of them.
- Okay, cool.

00:20:22.244 --> 00:20:25.495
People, well, okay, so
one person's asking,

00:20:25.495 --> 00:20:26.982
how do you get in the
zone so you can be the

00:20:26.982 --> 00:20:28.526
Michael Jordan of productivity?

00:20:28.526 --> 00:20:29.663
What do you do to get in the zone?

00:20:29.663 --> 00:20:30.774
- Okay, we're going to talk about that.

00:20:30.774 --> 00:20:31.850
It's a good question.

00:20:31.850 --> 00:20:34.646
But, I can dive in,
but let me wait for the

00:20:34.646 --> 00:20:38.530
third tip, but it's a very good question,

00:20:38.530 --> 00:20:41.130
and it's very important to
get yourself in the zone,

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:42.790
because when you're in the zone,

00:20:42.790 --> 00:20:46.390
you're three times more productive, right?

00:20:46.390 --> 00:20:49.223
So the second part of my five tips

00:20:51.398 --> 00:20:54.099
dives into how this happens.

00:20:54.099 --> 00:20:56.815
So number two is strategically
scheduling everything.

00:20:56.815 --> 00:20:58.944
When you get everything out of your head,

00:20:58.944 --> 00:21:00.803
and you put it on paper
and you delegate and sell

00:21:00.803 --> 00:21:03.439
yourself on what you're doing
and what you shouldn't do,

00:21:03.439 --> 00:21:04.624
that's when you start getting

00:21:04.624 --> 00:21:06.435
more motivation to follow through.

00:21:06.435 --> 00:21:08.855
So you have to have a seven-day review.

00:21:08.855 --> 00:21:10.542
You have to think about,
in the last seven days,

00:21:10.542 --> 00:21:13.869
how your week was, what you did well,

00:21:13.869 --> 00:21:15.717
what you didn't do well.

00:21:15.717 --> 00:21:17.540
When were you in the zone?

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:18.939
When were you distracted?

00:21:18.939 --> 00:21:21.191
When were you at your best?

00:21:21.191 --> 00:21:25.254
I always, every single week of every year

00:21:25.254 --> 00:21:28.353
in the last three years,
I've planned my weeks.

00:21:28.353 --> 00:21:30.444
It's a non-negotiable for me.

00:21:30.444 --> 00:21:31.506
Because think about it, guys.

00:21:31.506 --> 00:21:33.732
If you invest your past mistakes

00:21:33.732 --> 00:21:35.224
into your future preparation,

00:21:35.224 --> 00:21:36.721
you'll never have two bad weeks.

00:21:36.721 --> 00:21:38.126
Here's a crazy fact that you,

00:21:38.126 --> 00:21:40.048
you brought up Michael Jordan.

00:21:40.048 --> 00:21:41.795
Michael Jordan averaged
around 30 points a game

00:21:41.795 --> 00:21:45.353
his whole career, and
whenever he had a game

00:21:45.353 --> 00:21:47.964
that was less than 20
points, that's not that good

00:21:47.964 --> 00:21:50.595
for Michael Jordan, like 13, 14 points.

00:21:50.595 --> 00:21:53.712
Whenever he had a game
less than 20 points,

00:21:53.712 --> 00:21:56.629
his next game, he averaged over 40.

00:21:57.747 --> 00:22:00.214
Now, let me tell you what
this means productivity-wise.

00:22:00.214 --> 00:22:04.403
Michael Jordan never had two
bad games in his entire career.

00:22:04.403 --> 00:22:06.640
Never, not once. Okay?

00:22:06.640 --> 00:22:07.473
Why?

00:22:07.473 --> 00:22:10.617
Because when he had a bad
game, what do you think he did?

00:22:10.617 --> 00:22:11.994
Do you think he went out and drank beer?

00:22:11.994 --> 00:22:13.167
No, he studied the game.

00:22:13.167 --> 00:22:14.000
He studied the film.

00:22:14.000 --> 00:22:15.274
He asked himself what he did different.

00:22:15.274 --> 00:22:16.377
He watched the videos.

00:22:16.377 --> 00:22:17.664
He was tough on himself.

00:22:17.664 --> 00:22:18.680
He went back to the gym.

00:22:18.680 --> 00:22:19.513
He worked out more.

00:22:19.513 --> 00:22:22.289
He focused on his weaknesses
to turn them into strengths.

00:22:22.289 --> 00:22:23.687
Most entrepreneurs have a bad week,

00:22:23.687 --> 00:22:26.021
ah, whatever, it shouldn't happen again.

00:22:26.021 --> 00:22:27.729
And it happens again and again.

00:22:27.729 --> 00:22:28.908
That's why I don't understand how people

00:22:28.908 --> 00:22:30.719
have bad years and then another bad year.

00:22:30.719 --> 00:22:32.601
How is that humanly possible?

00:22:32.601 --> 00:22:34.650
If you don't invest your
time into your mistakes

00:22:34.650 --> 00:22:36.471
and make them better for the future.

00:22:36.471 --> 00:22:38.075
So that's why I get so passionate,

00:22:38.075 --> 00:22:40.194
because you got to review your weeks.

00:22:40.194 --> 00:22:42.377
Now, here's what you put
in your schedule first.

00:22:42.377 --> 00:22:44.326
Everything you can't change.

00:22:44.326 --> 00:22:47.588
Whatever you can't change,
like business meetings,

00:22:47.588 --> 00:22:50.869
calls with your team, maybe if
you're at a nine to five now,

00:22:50.869 --> 00:22:52.930
you obviously can't change that, right?

00:22:52.930 --> 00:22:56.390
Then, you put in what are you 100%

00:22:56.390 --> 00:22:59.685
committed to making happen no matter what.

00:22:59.685 --> 00:23:01.701
Whether, if you're in the
stage where you're not making

00:23:01.701 --> 00:23:04.656
much money, it needs to be
profit-producing activities.

00:23:04.656 --> 00:23:07.669
So what are your top three
profit-producing activities

00:23:07.669 --> 00:23:09.955
that are proven to make you money?

00:23:09.955 --> 00:23:11.152
Put that in your schedule first.

00:23:11.152 --> 00:23:13.044
You would not believe,
Evan, how many entrepreneurs

00:23:13.044 --> 00:23:16.049
I talk to at events and
at places, where they're

00:23:16.049 --> 00:23:17.837
walking me through
everything they're doing

00:23:17.837 --> 00:23:19.883
for the week, and they
have like a thousand things

00:23:19.883 --> 00:23:21.884
on their agenda, but
none of them make money.

00:23:21.884 --> 00:23:23.058
Then they're like, how do I make money?

00:23:23.058 --> 00:23:25.682
Well, you should probably
do things that make money,

00:23:25.682 --> 00:23:27.352
because everything you're
doing is not making money.

00:23:27.352 --> 00:23:28.185
It's the busy work.

00:23:28.185 --> 00:23:29.269
It's the easy stuff.

00:23:29.269 --> 00:23:31.150
A lot of people don't
want to do the one or two

00:23:31.150 --> 00:23:33.075
things that will actually help them.

00:23:33.075 --> 00:23:36.402
So for me I also add in my schedule,

00:23:36.402 --> 00:23:38.241
who am I going to reach out to?

00:23:38.241 --> 00:23:40.711
Who am I going to connect with
that can cut my learning curve

00:23:40.711 --> 00:23:44.071
in half, that can help me
get to my goals quicker?

00:23:44.071 --> 00:23:45.726
So put in your schedule what you're

00:23:45.726 --> 00:23:46.806
committed to making happen.

00:23:46.806 --> 00:23:49.103
Put in your schedule your non-negotiables,

00:23:49.103 --> 00:23:51.357
something you're committed
to, whether it's your health,

00:23:51.357 --> 00:23:54.728
maybe it's working out four
days a week, maybe it's

00:23:54.728 --> 00:23:56.947
alone time with you and
your wife or husband

00:23:56.947 --> 00:23:59.827
or significant other, maybe
it's getting a massage

00:23:59.827 --> 00:24:02.241
once a week to work on your peace of mind.

00:24:02.241 --> 00:24:03.912
I don't know, but you got
to strategically put it

00:24:03.912 --> 00:24:06.665
in your schedule, because
the trick to productivity

00:24:06.665 --> 00:24:09.103
and to get in the zone
is deciding what you're

00:24:09.103 --> 00:24:13.886
going to work on at some point
other than in the moment,

00:24:13.886 --> 00:24:16.563
and then practicing the
high-value work over and over

00:24:16.563 --> 00:24:19.400
'til it's habitual and automatic.

00:24:19.400 --> 00:24:22.667
So, as far as number three,
and I'm going to answer

00:24:22.667 --> 00:24:24.010
that question, "How do
you get in the zone?"

00:24:24.010 --> 00:24:26.141
Here's exactly how I get in the zone,

00:24:26.141 --> 00:24:27.128
and Evan already hit on it.

00:24:27.128 --> 00:24:28.649
It's the prizefighter routine,
but it's understanding

00:24:28.649 --> 00:24:31.411
about how to seize each day.

00:24:31.411 --> 00:24:32.712
You only get each day.

00:24:32.712 --> 00:24:36.311
Like, maximize your 24 hours,
and the rest of your life

00:24:36.311 --> 00:24:38.546
will take care of itself
if you understand this.

00:24:38.546 --> 00:24:41.501
So the first thing is you
have to get clear on what

00:24:41.501 --> 00:24:44.328
morning routine is most effective for you.

00:24:44.328 --> 00:24:47.394
You don't need to have 10
steps to a morning routine.

00:24:47.394 --> 00:24:48.510
You don't need that.

00:24:48.510 --> 00:24:50.262
You just want to focus on the outcome.

00:24:50.262 --> 00:24:52.165
What's the purpose of a morning routine?

00:24:52.165 --> 00:24:52.998
There's two things.

00:24:52.998 --> 00:24:56.672
One, confidence, make
sure you're in a confident

00:24:56.672 --> 00:24:58.599
and a courageous state of mind.

00:24:58.599 --> 00:25:00.368
So whatever you have to
do to get in the right

00:25:00.368 --> 00:25:03.684
state of mind, whether it's
working out, reading a book,

00:25:03.684 --> 00:25:05.739
writing in your journal,
meditating, I mean there's

00:25:05.739 --> 00:25:08.589
a thousand things you
could do in the morning,

00:25:08.589 --> 00:25:10.400
and if you talk to 10 entrepreneurs,

00:25:10.400 --> 00:25:11.939
all their routines are different.

00:25:11.939 --> 00:25:15.603
Mine's different than
Evan's, but the reality is,

00:25:15.603 --> 00:25:18.170
it gets us in the zone
when we start our day,

00:25:18.170 --> 00:25:19.522
so they're both correct.

00:25:19.522 --> 00:25:20.875
So the first thing is
get yourself in a better

00:25:20.875 --> 00:25:24.219
state of mind, and the second
thing is having intention

00:25:24.219 --> 00:25:26.425
and making sure you know
exactly what you're doing

00:25:26.425 --> 00:25:28.875
that day and you put
your activities in order

00:25:28.875 --> 00:25:31.870
highest value first, okay?

00:25:31.870 --> 00:25:33.641
That's the purpose of a morning routine.

00:25:33.641 --> 00:25:37.059
Next, I visualize and I
define my perfect day.

00:25:37.059 --> 00:25:40.421
This sounded corny when I first
heard it, just being honest.

00:25:40.421 --> 00:25:41.837
I was like, I'm not going
to visualize my perfect day.

00:25:41.837 --> 00:25:43.947
That sounds horrible,
that's a waste of time.

00:25:43.947 --> 00:25:44.792
But then I actually did it.

00:25:44.792 --> 00:25:46.336
It's one thing to say
something's a waste of time,

00:25:46.336 --> 00:25:48.002
it's another thing to actually do it.

00:25:48.002 --> 00:25:50.352
I visualize, I think
about my ideal outcome,

00:25:50.352 --> 00:25:52.809
how I'm going to feel
at the end of the day,

00:25:52.809 --> 00:25:55.204
what my ideal day looks like, and, man,

00:25:55.204 --> 00:25:59.528
it gets me so focused and
excited to complete that day.

00:25:59.528 --> 00:26:02.474
And then I ask myself three
questions, and this is all,

00:26:02.474 --> 00:26:05.011
guys, 30 to 45 minutes.

00:26:05.011 --> 00:26:07.571
What am I most excited about for the day?

00:26:07.571 --> 00:26:08.404
And if you don't have anything

00:26:08.404 --> 00:26:10.332
that you're excited
about, create something.

00:26:10.332 --> 00:26:12.492
What am I extremely grateful for?

00:26:12.492 --> 00:26:14.558
It's impossible to be
frustrated when you're grateful,

00:26:14.558 --> 00:26:16.391
by the way, so I always get grateful

00:26:16.391 --> 00:26:18.956
so I'm not frustrated or discouraged.

00:26:18.956 --> 00:26:21.986
And then what am I 100%
committed to make happen?

00:26:21.986 --> 00:26:25.313
And once I do that, I finally
have clarity for my day,

00:26:25.313 --> 00:26:27.682
and then it's the 60, 20,
60, where it's 60 minutes

00:26:27.682 --> 00:26:32.183
no interruptions, no
distractions, straight focus

00:26:32.183 --> 00:26:33.627
on my highest-value activity,
whether it's writing

00:26:33.627 --> 00:26:35.934
in my book, creating
something for my mix tape

00:26:35.934 --> 00:26:38.569
for one of my programs, whatever it is.

00:26:38.569 --> 00:26:40.321
Straight focus for 60 minutes.

00:26:40.321 --> 00:26:43.217
Then I take a 15, 20 minute break.

00:26:43.217 --> 00:26:45.700
I either go walk around
the block, shoot some hoops

00:26:45.700 --> 00:26:47.598
down the street, I watch a YouTube video.

00:26:47.598 --> 00:26:51.005
You got to do something unrelated,
but the reality is here,

00:26:51.005 --> 00:26:53.282
you ought to get out
of that state of mind,

00:26:53.282 --> 00:26:56.886
and then when you're back
for the next 60 minute block,

00:26:56.886 --> 00:26:59.161
now you want to make sure
you're fully focused again

00:26:59.161 --> 00:27:02.297
in a new state of mind
and then sell yourself

00:27:02.297 --> 00:27:04.230
on the activity that you're doing.

00:27:04.230 --> 00:27:07.868
Sell yourself on whatever
you have planned.

00:27:07.868 --> 00:27:10.354
If you're not sold on
the activity at hand,

00:27:10.354 --> 00:27:12.287
that's when people procrastinate.

00:27:12.287 --> 00:27:15.346
You will never procrastinate
if you fully sell yourself

00:27:15.346 --> 00:27:17.470
on why you're doing what you're doing.

00:27:17.470 --> 00:27:19.131
If you don't feel like
doing something, Evan,

00:27:19.131 --> 00:27:22.868
maybe this video or whatever,
I almost guarantee it,

00:27:22.868 --> 00:27:24.325
you think about why you're doing it.

00:27:24.325 --> 00:27:26.724
You don't care how you feel in the moment

00:27:26.724 --> 00:27:28.855
because you're doing it
for you, for your legacy,

00:27:28.855 --> 00:27:30.297
for your family, to have freedom,

00:27:30.297 --> 00:27:32.067
for income, peace of mind.

00:27:32.067 --> 00:27:33.564
So if it's sold, you're
like, it doesn't matter

00:27:33.564 --> 00:27:34.755
how I feel, I'm doing it.

00:27:34.755 --> 00:27:36.334
But a lot of people don't sell themselves

00:27:36.334 --> 00:27:37.745
on what they're doing.

00:27:37.745 --> 00:27:39.213
And they're not really sold on it,

00:27:39.213 --> 00:27:40.496
they're kind of doing it half-ass,

00:27:40.496 --> 00:27:43.352
so that's when they
procrastinate and procrastinate.

00:27:43.352 --> 00:27:44.932
So if you want to get in the zone,

00:27:44.932 --> 00:27:47.548
you got to sell yourself
on everything you're doing

00:27:47.548 --> 00:27:50.215
and you need to make sure you
get in the right state of mind

00:27:50.215 --> 00:27:52.148
before you take something on.

00:27:52.148 --> 00:27:54.434
And how you get in the zone is you work

00:27:54.434 --> 00:27:56.938
straight for 20, 23 minutes.

00:27:56.938 --> 00:27:58.081
That's how you get in the zone.

00:27:58.081 --> 00:28:00.483
Most people, before they
even get to 20 minutes,

00:28:00.483 --> 00:28:03.409
they're distracted, and it
takes 20 minutes to get back

00:28:03.409 --> 00:28:05.625
in the zone, so they're
never actually in the zone,

00:28:05.625 --> 00:28:06.938
because they're always distracted.

00:28:06.938 --> 00:28:08.936
They're going from
distraction to distraction,

00:28:08.936 --> 00:28:10.986
versus from in the zone to in the zone.

00:28:10.986 --> 00:28:13.389
So hopefully that answered
some of the questions,

00:28:13.389 --> 00:28:15.385
but this is something you
can tell I'm very passionate

00:28:15.385 --> 00:28:18.193
about because I see
people wasting their lives

00:28:18.193 --> 00:28:21.185
because they're not taking
the time to be disciplined.

00:28:21.185 --> 00:28:23.321
Instead, they're working all the time.

00:28:23.321 --> 00:28:25.688
So I could go on for a long time.

00:28:25.688 --> 00:28:27.935
Any other questions?

00:28:27.935 --> 00:28:28.768
- Dude, it's blowing up!

00:28:28.768 --> 00:28:29.601
It's crazy!

00:28:29.601 --> 00:28:30.776
Any other questions.

00:28:30.776 --> 00:28:31.955
- I appreciate you guys, by the way.

00:28:31.955 --> 00:28:34.521
- It's like it's off the page, man.

00:28:34.521 --> 00:28:36.492
I have to pick which ones come up.

00:28:36.492 --> 00:28:38.602
Uh, okay. This is interesting.

00:28:38.602 --> 00:28:39.786
Esther.

00:28:39.786 --> 00:28:43.838
Esther is saying, how do
you, this is about execution.

00:28:43.838 --> 00:28:47.557
How do you lose the
fear/insecurity so that you

00:28:47.557 --> 00:28:49.083
can go out and execute?

00:28:49.083 --> 00:28:50.181
- Yeah. Couple things.

00:28:50.181 --> 00:28:53.968
One, you have to be around,
and I've gone through this.

00:28:53.968 --> 00:28:56.621
You have to be around, the
reason people don't execute

00:28:56.621 --> 00:28:59.941
sometimes, Evan, is they
don't have certainty

00:28:59.941 --> 00:29:01.579
that it's going to work.

00:29:01.579 --> 00:29:03.338
That's why a lot of people
love the nine to five,

00:29:03.338 --> 00:29:04.171
because there's certainty.

00:29:04.171 --> 00:29:05.398
I'm going to get paid.

00:29:05.398 --> 00:29:06.615
It's certain, right?

00:29:06.615 --> 00:29:09.415
In entrepreneurship, there's no certainty.

00:29:09.415 --> 00:29:14.100
So you have to increase your
certainty by a couple things.

00:29:14.100 --> 00:29:17.182
When your certainty's increased,
like if I told you, Evan,

00:29:17.182 --> 00:29:20.184
when you started, hey, when
you do this YouTube thing,

00:29:20.184 --> 00:29:22.419
you will get two thousand
subscribers a day.

00:29:22.419 --> 00:29:23.450
You're going to have a million subscribers

00:29:23.450 --> 00:29:24.851
in exactly this time.

00:29:24.851 --> 00:29:25.861
You're going to have this, this, this.

00:29:25.861 --> 00:29:26.694
This is the money coming in.

00:29:26.694 --> 00:29:28.547
You'd be like, oh, my God, that's easier.

00:29:28.547 --> 00:29:32.508
But when you first started,
you didn't have that certainty.

00:29:32.508 --> 00:29:35.108
You had to create the certainty
by getting the results.

00:29:35.108 --> 00:29:37.627
So here's a couple things
that you can do to increase

00:29:37.627 --> 00:29:39.346
your certainty, which then increases

00:29:39.346 --> 00:29:41.018
your chances of execution.

00:29:41.018 --> 00:29:43.949
One, do your due diligence, okay?

00:29:43.949 --> 00:29:45.888
Do the research on what industry you're in

00:29:45.888 --> 00:29:47.716
or what you're working
on to make sure you have

00:29:47.716 --> 00:29:49.481
the best information to follow.

00:29:49.481 --> 00:29:53.165
Two, get around other
people that are executors.

00:29:53.165 --> 00:29:55.580
A lot of people that aren't executing,

00:29:55.580 --> 00:29:58.681
every single person, and this is done

00:29:58.681 --> 00:30:00.590
with a lot of study and me just dealing

00:30:00.590 --> 00:30:02.918
with a lot of entrepreneurs in person.

00:30:02.918 --> 00:30:05.149
A lot of people that aren't executing,

00:30:05.149 --> 00:30:07.999
the five people they're around the most,

00:30:07.999 --> 00:30:09.982
they don't execute either.

00:30:09.982 --> 00:30:12.103
So if you're around other executors,

00:30:12.103 --> 00:30:13.775
other people taking big action,

00:30:13.775 --> 00:30:15.488
other people thinking bigger,

00:30:15.488 --> 00:30:19.155
it's a lot easier for
you to execute, right?

00:30:20.271 --> 00:30:21.937
And then three, like I just said.

00:30:21.937 --> 00:30:23.138
You might have already got the answer.

00:30:23.138 --> 00:30:27.057
Sell yourself before you
start taking that action.

00:30:27.057 --> 00:30:28.439
So if it's like, okay, you want to...

00:30:28.439 --> 00:30:29.588
For me, I'll tell ya.

00:30:29.588 --> 00:30:32.552
My book, Six Months to Six
Figures, I'm so blessed

00:30:32.552 --> 00:30:34.749
it's sold close to 200,000 copies.

00:30:34.749 --> 00:30:36.151
It's gone crazy, right?

00:30:36.151 --> 00:30:38.197
I didn't expect that.

00:30:38.197 --> 00:30:41.151
When I was writing the book, it was hell.

00:30:41.151 --> 00:30:43.368
A, you don't get paid for
writing a book until way later.

00:30:43.368 --> 00:30:44.603
B, it's hard.

00:30:44.603 --> 00:30:47.285
C, I'm like type A, I'm
freaking out, I'm jumping.

00:30:47.285 --> 00:30:48.597
I did like 30 pushups before this

00:30:48.597 --> 00:30:50.585
interview to get fired up.

00:30:50.585 --> 00:30:55.089
But the reality is, I had to
sell myself a thousand times.

00:30:55.089 --> 00:30:57.818
That's the only reason I
got it done and executed.

00:30:57.818 --> 00:31:00.842
I said, you know, I just got
to visualize how it's going to

00:31:00.842 --> 00:31:03.228
feel to get this book
done, to get this book

00:31:03.228 --> 00:31:05.443
in someone's hands, and
I just kept thinking

00:31:05.443 --> 00:31:08.845
about people saying, your
book changed my life.

00:31:08.845 --> 00:31:11.442
Because of your book, I did not give up,

00:31:11.442 --> 00:31:13.362
I didn't commit suicide, all these things.

00:31:13.362 --> 00:31:17.235
That drove me, and I
couldn't stop the book

00:31:17.235 --> 00:31:18.186
when I thought about that.

00:31:18.186 --> 00:31:20.376
But most people think
about what they have to do

00:31:20.376 --> 00:31:21.726
versus what they want.

00:31:21.726 --> 00:31:24.061
So don't think about all you have to do.

00:31:24.061 --> 00:31:26.899
Think about what you want
and your ideal outcome,

00:31:26.899 --> 00:31:29.258
and it's just little bits and pieces.

00:31:29.258 --> 00:31:32.009
Take a little more action
than the day before.

00:31:32.009 --> 00:31:34.735
Take a little more action
the next day than today.

00:31:34.735 --> 00:31:37.643
Take a little more action
in two days than tomorrow.

00:31:37.643 --> 00:31:41.193
And if you can do that, mixed
with doing your due diligence,

00:31:41.193 --> 00:31:43.944
getting around higher-level
people, and making

00:31:43.944 --> 00:31:46.464
the tougher decisions in
the moments, it's going to

00:31:46.464 --> 00:31:49.970
give you the confidence to be
able to take bigger action.

00:31:49.970 --> 00:31:51.676
But sometimes people
that don't take action,

00:31:51.676 --> 00:31:54.496
